+# HARNESS_LOG — defect: coaching reply fails to parse
+
+## Plan
+- Symptom: "could not read the reply" intermittently, when reply is long/multi-line.
+- Files read: lib/claude-json.ts, lib/claude-json.test.ts; callers app/api/coach/reflect/route.ts,
+  app/api/dasha/route.ts.
+- Suspected root cause: `prepareJsonString` (lib/claude-json.ts:36) replaces EVERY bare `\n`/`\t`
+  with a literal `\\n`/`\\t`, including structural whitespace between tokens. Pretty-printed JSON
+  (`{\n  "a": ...`) becomes `{\n  "a"` with a literal backslash outside a string -> JSON.parse throws.
+  Single-line replies parse fine, hence "sometimes".
+  Also `\r` inside strings is never escaped.
+- Fix: replace the blind regex with a small string-aware scanner that escapes raw `\n`, `\r`, `\t`
+  only while inside a JSON string literal (tracking `\` escapes), leaving structural whitespace alone.
+  Keep the lastIndexOf("}") slicing as-is (existing KNOWN LIMITATION test asserts it).
+- Add a new test file lib/claude-json.multiline.test.ts with a realistic long multi-line coaching reply.
+- Verify: npx vitest run, npx tsc --noEmit.
+
+## Log
+- Change 1: lib/claude-json.ts — replaced blind `\n`/`\t` regex escape with string-aware
+  `escapeControlCharsInStrings` (escapes raw \n, \r, \t only inside string literals).
+- Change 2: added lib/claude-json.multiline.test.ts (long fenced pretty-printed reply with
+  multi-line/CRLF/tab string values; CRLF between tokens; escaped backslash before quote).
+- `npx vitest run` -> Test Files 38 passed (38), Tests 283 passed (283).
+- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0, no output.
+- NOT RUN: tests against the pre-fix code (git stash command needed approval and was not approved),
+  so "new/existing tests fail on old code" is reasoned, not observed.
